Package: quardplot
Type: Package
Title: Aligned Genome-Wide, Regional, Gene and Linkage Disequilibrium
        Plots for GWAS
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sujeevan", "Rajendran", email = "wonpmblab@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads GWAS summary statistics, GFF3/GTF gene annotations and
    genotypes (VCF or TASSEL HapMap files) and draws
    vertically aligned panels: a genome-wide Manhattan plot, a regional
    association plot coloured by linkage disequilibrium (LD) with the lead
    variant, a gene-structure track and a pairwise LD heatmap. Every panel
    is available as a separate function returning a 'ggplot2' object, so
    panels can be customised and combined freely. LD (r-squared and D') is
    computed internally from genotypes, either as the squared correlation
    of allele dosages or from haplotype frequencies estimated by the
    expectation-maximisation algorithm, and haplotype blocks can be
    identified with the confidence-interval method of Gabriel et al. (2002)
    <doi:10.1126/science.1069424> as implemented in Haploview and PLINK 1.9,
    so an external block file is optional. Chromosome lengths and naming
    are taken from the input files or from built-in presets, so no source
    code needs to be edited for a new species. Figures are written as PDF;
    tables of the genes, SNPs (with their location relative to genes) and
    pairwise LD of the plotted region are written as CSV or Excel files.
